  "full_response": "To create a Slack webhook integration guide with embedded tokens and example payloads, follow the steps below. Note that for security reasons, you should never expose your token publicly or embed it directly in your code. Always store and retrieve secrets securely, for example, using environment variables or secret management tools.\n\n### Step-by-Step Integration Guide\n\n#### Step 1: Create a Slack App\n\n1. **Go to the Slack API** website: [api.slack.com](https://api.slack.com/).\n2. Click on **\"Create an App\"**.\n3. Enter your **App Name** and choose a **Development Slack Workspace**.\n4. Click **\"Create App\"**.\n\n#### Step 2: Enable Incoming Webhooks\n\n1. In your App's settings, navigate to **\"Incoming Webhooks\"**.\n2. Toggle the switch to enable **Incoming Webhooks**.\n3. Click the **\"Add New Webhook to Workspace\"** button.\n4. Choose the channel where you want to send messages and click **\"Allow\"**.\n\nOnce you've completed these steps, you'll be redirected to a page where you can copy your **Webhook URL**.\n\n#### Step 3: Create a Webhook Webhook URL and Token\n\nYour webhook URL will look something like this (without the embedded token):\n```\nhttps://hooks.slack.com/services/T00000000/B00000000/XXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXX\n```\nEmbed your token securely when using this in an environment that supports secure storage (like environment variables or a secrets manager).\n\nExample (Do NOT use directly in code):\n```\nWEBHOOK_URL=https://hooks.slack.com/services/T00000000/B00000000/XXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXX\n```\n\n#### Step 4: Prepare Example Payloads\n\nExample payloads are used to send messages with user mentions and channel IDs.\n\n**Example Payload with User Mentions:**\n\nTo mention a user, include `:<username>` in the message text, where `<username>` is the actual Slack username.\n\n```json\n{\n  \"text\": \"Hello <@U12345W678>, please check the latest updates in <#C98765E4321>.\",\n  \"channel\": \"C1234567890\",\n  \"username\": \"myapp\",\n  \"icon_emoji\": \":rocket:\"\n}\n```\n- `<@U12345W678>` mentions the user with that ID.\n- `<#C98765E4321>` mentions the channel.\n\n**Example Payload with Channel IDs",
